      "title": "Dividend reduced to ₹2.00",
      "body": "Dividend of ₹2.00 is 33% lower than last year. Ex-date: 4th August 2026 Payment date: 10th September 2026 Dividend yield will be 0.2%, which is lower than the industry average of 0.9%. Sustainability & Growth Dividend is covered by earnings (3% earnings payout ratio) but the company has no free cash flows available, indicating it may be using cash reserves or debt to pay the dividend. The dividend has increased by an average of 4.6% per year over the past 9 years. However, payments have been volatile during that time. The company's earnings per share (EPS) would need to decline by 97% to shift the payout ratio to a potentially unsustainable range, which is more than the 27% EPS decline seen over the last 5 years.",
